# Rank 1917 / CVE-2024-21636: ViewComponent's render pipeline returned the
# component's markup without an HTML-escape step (CWE-79). render_in in
# lib/view_component/base.rb did
#
#   render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + output_postamble
#
# so a component whose call method interpolates request data -- the documented
# way to author a component -- had that output inserted into the page raw.
# The fixing commit c43d8bafa7 is the 2.x backport: render_in now routes through
# safe_render_template_for and safe_output_postamble, whose shared helper
# maybe_escape_html returns the text untouched when it is html_safe?
# and otherwise wraps it in html_escape. : the commit is the
# fixing change, the vulnerable concatenation is present at its parent, and the
# remediation is present at the commit itself.
#
# ATTENTION, attribution gap. Nothing labels the render pipeline at either
# revision: vyql match on base.rb shows the only HtmlRender sink is the
# unrelated render-delegation helper (base.rb:197 -> 202 at the vulnerable revision,
# 202 -> 207 after the pure line shift), and a bounded scan of the checkout
# reports the same 17 findings at both revisions. The weakness is not a
# dataflow inside the library -- the untrusted bytes enter through
# application-authored components, and sink positions exist only at
# args/args.any/node/call, never at a return -- so the taint rule cannot fire,
# and a presence binding on the render entry cannot discriminate: every
# remediated revision still calls render_template_for (inside
# safe_render_template_for at this fix, and directly inside render_in on
# current main, which keeps render_template_for(...).to_s with the escaping
# html_escape two helpers away), while the generic escape API lives outside
# the function the fixed revision guards. That is the measured endpointGuarded family
# (function-local control attribution: ranks 1377/1389/1399 Go, 1397 Python,
# 1364 Rust, 1372 TypeScript, 1394 PHP, 1437 C; identical-shape non-detection
# at 1331), and the 1380 counterweight fails because the fixed revision leaves no
# API-documented control call in render_in -- only its own safe_* helpers and
# output_postamble.blank?, an allocation micro-optimization with no security
# meaning, so keying on its absence is the rank-1394 helper-name trap. The
# adjacent application shape is covered but version-blind: params ->
# MessageComponent.new -> render(component) reports VYQL-INJ-004 at high on a
# two-file probe, yet the same application code is safe once the framework
# escapes, so that finding cannot track this fix. Not an ENGINE-GAPS.md entry:
# what is missing is either a return-position render sink with a
# framework-output trust model or cross-function control attribution, both
# vocabulary/engine design rather than a mechanical change.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-analysis-gap, both revisions rejected

test "rank1917: the render entry returns template output concatenated with the postamble, unescaped"
  lang ruby
  file lib/view_component/base.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  reject VYQL-INJ-204
  code
  ```
  module ViewComponent
    class Base < ActionView::Base
      def render_in(view_context, &block)
        @view_context = view_context

        @lookup_context ||= view_context.lookup_context

        # For template variants (+phone, +desktop, etc.)
        @__vc_variant ||= @lookup_context.variants.first

        @__vc_render_in_block = block

        before_render

        if render?
          render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + output_postamble
        else
          ""
        end
      end

      # Optional content to be returned after the rendered template.
      #
      # @return [String]
      def output_postamble
        ""
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1917: the render entry escapes template output and postamble unless html_safe"
  lang ruby
  file lib/view_component/base.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  reject VYQL-INJ-204
  code
  ```
  module ViewComponent
    class Base < ActionView::Base
      def render_in(view_context, &block)
        @view_context = view_context

        @lookup_context ||= view_context.lookup_context

        @__vc_variant ||= @lookup_context.variants.first

        @__vc_render_in_block = block

        before_render

        if render?
          # Avoid allocating new string when output_postamble is blank
          if output_postamble.blank?
            safe_render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s
          else
            safe_render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + safe_output_postamble
          end
        else
          ""
        end
      end

      def maybe_escape_html(text)
        return text if request && !request.format.html?
        return text if text.blank?

        if text.html_safe?
          text
        else
          yield
          html_escape(text)
        end
      end

      def safe_render_template_for(variant)
        if compiler.renders_template_for_variant?(variant)
          render_template_for(variant)
        else
          maybe_escape_html(render_template_for(variant)) do
            Kernel.warn("WARNING: The #{self.class} component rendered HTML-unsafe output. The output will be automatically escaped, but you may want to investigate.")
          end
        end
      end

      def safe_output_postamble
        maybe_escape_html(output_postamble) do
          Kernel.warn("WARNING: The #{self.class} component was provided an HTML-unsafe postamble. The postamble will be automatically escaped, but you may want to investigate.")
        end
      end

      def output_postamble
        @@default_output_postamble ||= "".html_safe
      end
    end
  end
  ```
